r-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a Java program using synchronized threads, which demonstrates producer consumerconcept.</p><p data-ref="01722b77-3e26-4e6b-a9a1-4f581d2f01aa" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="052df6dd-f583-440f-bb2a-994c6c11da48"></p><p data-ref="8adb1e07-453c-4982-85e6-42b5f5696b50" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">The Producer-Consumer problem is a classic synchronization problem in computer science. It involves two types of threads:</p><ul data-ref="158077fd-0b5f-4bde-99d2-37e19e1073d8" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="276a33d3-de49-4d0c-9e55-adbc6937a272"><strong data-ref="47219ad1-5162-4cd9-8b8e-8ad7febf47ec">Producer</strong>: This thread generates data (e.g., items) and places it in a shared resource (like a buffer).</li><li data-ref="c1d8b6d5-9555-4e1c-852c-7a652004f197"><strong data-ref="654aa20e-3061-4401-a809-5930a5b8831a">Consumer</strong>: This thread takes data (items) from the shared resource for processing or consumption.</li></ul><p data-ref="19e56b36-a179-4c9f-813f-82afaddcb5e8" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="9430707b-0dd0-49ec-aab8-514a881d91ba"></p><p data-ref="b0f6632f-b79c-4972-b3d1-98bc52b506e6" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">The problem revolves around coordinating these threads such that:</p><ul data-ref="8cd4a33a-c63e-4eb8-8123-6defe528020a" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="1bd293cb-07ad-41e6-864f-59ad6d4d496e">The producer does not produce when the buffer is full.</li><li data-ref="cb79ad3e-d19f-49c4-ad43-eaaf831befb7">The consumer does not consume when the buffer is empty.</li><li data-ref="fa203ecf-db79-4716-b24a-fea9429895d4">Both threads operate safely without corrupting the shared resource.</li></ul><p data-ref="57bcd002-1ac4-4500-98c3-ad0dc4666621" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="e1b08afb-074b-4898-a5ce-e576e9b078a6"></p><p data-ref="9d26f671-0e88-4794-abc7-f041aca0a619" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">To achieve synchronization in Java, we can use the synchronized keyword along with wait and notify methods to control the interaction between the threads.</p><p data-ref="b0f0ceaa-e3c4-4376-ba75-bf0565d0aece" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="589ff5d3-952c-4073-b5d8-9daf53dbcd0a"></p><p data-ref="591155df-99ed-4bbf-b21c-6bf496eda97c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="287fd71e-4de7-4b99-a845-612a7998429b">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="0503243d-8142-41fd-b20c-9e7a940b548a" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="dc8e327f-3a75-4fa9-be41-c3b4840ab2a8">Prompt the user to enter an integer representing the number of items to produce along with a print statement <strong data-ref="a48fd244-8977-4db3-97ba-2456a4c04bed">"Enter the number of items to produce: " </strong></li></ul><p data-ref="c2e6f364-03ad-4f4e-9ac3-009381348be5" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="2a45d87b-2124-4cb2-a1d0-f0f8fa028a05"></p><p data-ref="b702ebcb-bd00-4c10-9b7d-e6d4558ed666" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="ff437641-6e94-47b6-a561-0e0cdb8cee57">Output Format:</strong></p><p data-ref="c83330ed-f9fc-4fe4-b207-2b4e7285a010" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Output should print the following:</p><ul data-ref="946995e0-ba91-40ec-9e20-abc0d5309b33" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="65148477-e9f8-47e0-a675-504e937944f4">Messages indicating the production of each item as &lt;Produced: {Produced item}&gt;</li><li data-ref="d47cc2c5-0614-405d-a61e-b65b1324b581">Messages indicating the consumption of each item as &lt;Consumed: {Consumed item}&gt;</li></ul></span></div><div class="mb-3" data-ref="8a75657a-f46d-4c54-be19-020828d3c923"><div class="ml-1 mb-3" data-ref="5bffd6a7-155c-456e-9724-c437c29b3f2e"><b style="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="de59065c-ea65-4218-9022-e5ee50153942" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Source Code: </b></div><div class="user-solution" style="page-break-inside: auto" data-ref="25f3de8e-3598-4b84-842d-3b57615e7aeb" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><div class="px-3 pt-2 pb-1" style="font-family: monospace !important;border-radius: 4px 4px 0 0; border: 1px solid black; break-after: avoid; page-break-after: avoid;" data-ref="49d99795-3c9e-4f11-8eb1-da75ba15f22b" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">q28802/ProducerConsumerDemo.java</div> <pre style="overflow: visible; border: 1px solid black; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 4px;" class="px-3 pt-2 pb-1" data-ref="9a80db06-1215-47bb-8b14-ad570c20f530" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">package q28802;
import java.util.LinkedList;
import java.util.Scanner;

// Write your code here...
class Buffer {
    private LinkedList&lt;Integer&gt; list = new LinkedList&lt;&gt;();
    private int capacity = 1;

    public synchronized void produce(int item) throws InterruptedException {
        while (list.size() == capacity) {
            wait();
        }
        list.add(item);
        System.out.println("Produced: " + item);
        notify();
    }

    public synchronized void consume() throws InterruptedException {
        while (list.isEmpty()) {
            wait();
        }
        int item = list.removeFirst();
        System.out.println("Consumed: " + item);
        notify();
    }
}

class Producer extends Thread {
    Buffer buffer;
    int n;

    Producer(Buffer buffer, int n) {
        this.buffer = buffer;
        this.n = n;
    }

    public void run() {
        try {
            for (int i = 1; i &lt;= n; i++) {
                buffer.produce(i);
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
        }
    }
}

class Consumer extends Thread {
    Buffer buffer;
    int n;

    Consumer(Buffer buffer, int n) {
        this.buffer = buffer;
        this.n = n;
    }

    public void run() {
        try {
            for (int i = 1; i &lt;= n; i++) {
                buffer.consume();
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
        }
    }
}


public class ProducerConsumerDemo {
	// Write your code here...
	    public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter the number of items to produce: ");
        int n = sc.nextInt();

        Buffer buffer = new Buffer();

        Producer producer = new Producer(buffer, n);
        Consumer consumer = new Consumer(buffer, n);

        producer.start();
        consumer.start();

        producer.join();
        consumer.join();

        sc.close();
