ata-ref="7b059433-72d9-415d-877a-31cba2302037" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="b4c2a53a-02f3-4f27-8dcf-364bcc4a1183"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="cab8236e-19c7-4209-8d84-2961459d8e16"><p data-ref="5a0e4344-2b8f-4ce0-8c67-e341bd1d7c23" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Create a Java program that demonstrates the use of user and daemon threads. Implement a class <strong data-ref="d5c08d3e-1203-41d7-94ac-95c85c46a306">WorkerThread</strong> that extends <strong data-ref="9d650a9c-574a-4a3b-88bc-330e9722c63b">Thread</strong> and overrides the <strong data-ref="7ab0d01f-c79f-4533-9239-b6974990e634">run</strong> method to simulate some work by printing messages and sleeping for a short duration.</p><p data-ref="0c23fbcf-a868-49f9-8ed4-835e04709f3a" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="380012ee-6d56-4c2b-8dcc-33dab14d9f68"></p><p data-ref="eebbc453-55f0-4afb-9dd1-ff52f85f0567" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">In the <strong data-ref="b586d8ab-d3cc-4625-9879-8b7068c3d2b2">DaemonThread</strong> class:</p><p data-ref="dfb7c132-fd09-4ee8-9289-200b77bbb61c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">1. Prompt the user to input the number of user threads and daemon threads.</p><p data-ref="38da68b6-c95c-416a-ab33-19d112aa00e2" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">2. Create and start the specified number of user threads and daemon threads.</p><ul data-ref="54badfae-ec3e-42fc-9ef7-b3fd94928abf" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="c712ff5c-4fd0-4599-a12e-acc21eb8469d"><strong data-ref="547bba81-c4e1-463f-96ea-2afbb5b8d8e3">User Threads: </strong>These threads will run to completion and are not interrupted by the main thread.<strong data-ref="6b0307fd-f3c7-4d56-8233-ab90ae248241">Daemon Threads:</strong> These threads will run in the background and may be terminated abruptly when the main thread exits.</li></ul><p data-ref="ab6f98aa-3667-4b1a-8b1b-4cb4f55e1e90" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">3. The main thread should print a message indicating its exit after creating the threads.</p><p data-ref="72beac0c-34af-4336-a137-414df0e1474d" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="147a6e2c-3b9a-4a57-a0bf-55967e8d75ff"></p><p data-ref="c709dc63-3689-4683-80b5-363658a53b8b" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="04a7ceaa-02d7-437b-b118-62540fbd8c0d">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="f6ae63cc-3b43-4aea-a9eb-e98134cfe05a" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="13008c47-8e81-41b9-9c37-8e4c4d2de3d3">The first line contains an integer specifying the number of user threads.</li><li data-ref="1b6351be-1cd8-492e-8999-b2f14c8d4c5f">The second line contains an integer specifying the number of daemon threads.</li></ul><p data-ref="2444670f-bf2c-4aee-8f83-41591b6f6202" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" da